{
  "_readme": [
    "THE ONLY PLACE PRICES, DATES AND AVAILABILITY ARE DEFINED.",
    "Both booking pages read it. Both Stripe charges are priced from it.",
    "",
    "SHAPE",
    "  products.<name>.defaults   base price, tiers, options, deposit rule",
    "  products.<name>.editions   one block per date; 'prices' overrides the defaults",
    "",
    "TIERS are the mutually exclusive choice. For the weekend that is the room;",
    "for the week it is the package. Weekend tier prices ADD to the base.",
    "The week has base 0, so its tier price IS the package price.",
    "",
    "AN EDITION CAN RESTRICT TIERS with \"tiers\": [\"full\"]. That enforces the",
    "",
    "'left' is places remaining. 0 shows as full and the server refuses the sale.",
    "It is manual — nothing decrements it on purchase. Buyers see it, so keep it true.",
    "",
    "Deploy after editing (wrangler deploy). This file is bundled into the Worker,",
    "so a JSON syntax error fails the build rather than breaking the live site.",
    "",
    "LEVEL — the bands below are PLACEHOLDERS. Get the real ones from your FPP",
    "coach: they know how M/F/Mixed categories actually play around Milfontes.",
    "'playtomic' is the machine-readable band (0-7 scale, 0.25 steps) and the one",
    "buyers outside Portugal will recognise. 'federation' holds the ladders that",
    "apply to that edition — drop a ladder entirely if it does not. An edition",
    "showing only 'm' reads as a men's edition, so list all three unless you mean it.",
    "",
    "DEPOSITS are off. 'deposit': null means full payment confirms the booking.",
    "Setting an object here ({ amount, balanceDueDays }) turns the option back on —",
    "but nothing invoices or chases a balance yet, so leave it null until that exists.",
    "",
    "IDs MUST BE UNIQUE and must be the edition's START DATE (YYYY-MM-DD).",
    "Two editions sharing an id is silent: the file is valid, it deploys, and the",
    "second one renders as a duplicate of the first instead of appearing."
  ],
